<title>UK: JKX Oil &amp; Gas H1 pretax loss widens.</title>
<headline>JKX Oil &amp; Gas H1 pretax loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.77 loss	    vs 1.26 loss</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.92 loss	    vs 0.5 loss</p>
<p> Turnover		   4.12		   vs n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - JKX Oil &amp; Gas Plc, which was floated in July 1995, focuses on development opportunities in the former Soviet Union. The group said comparisons with 1995 figures were not meaningful because there was no commercial production until the last quarter of 1995.  </p>
<p> Operating loss	   1.41		   vs 0.53</p>
<p> Interest receivable    0.37		   vs nil</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.10		   vs 0.002</p>
<p> Tax			  nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Retained loss	    0.92		   vs 0.48</p>
<p> Attributable	     1.21 loss	    vs 0.48 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm said the experience it had gained so far in the Ukraine and Georgia from developing fields and selling oil and gas placed it in a strong position to pursue its strategy in the former Soviet Union. The group reported average production of 5,700 barrels of oil equivalent per day for the period.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
